The STL is exported in its native frame (identity axes: x = the ~124 mm long bar the sensors are
arrayed across, y = height ~29 mm, z = depth ~26 mm with the front glass at z=0 and +z the lens
outward normal), which already matches the d435/d415 mesh convention -- no reorientation was applied.

Every pose in roqsim_sensors/models/realsense_d455/realsense_d455.xml and in the `frames:` block of
realsense_d455.manifest.yaml -- the mesh in camera_link, the `d455_color` camera at the colour
optical frame, the depth frames -- is read from the same repository's
realsense2_description/urdf/_d455.urdf.xacro by external/convert/build_realsense_devices.py, not
measured off the mesh.
